				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "NcAAqc+zQhKIZdoQ9VHzxQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Back in [[Hooking up your server]], I promised that the result of a cell can answer a live object. It’s time to make good on that promise! This is probably my favorite part of the whole thing."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "p5NrKsajRbGvp2UO1ZxLYA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "When a cell ends in an expression, the server wraps that expression before compiling it. The compiled program evaluates it, registers the result, and then does something slightly strange for a compiled program: it stays alive. It becomes the session’s value host, a small HTTP server inside the program that serves the value and its views. The runtime for this is `carp/src/notebook.carp`, which every cell is compiled with."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "Uv3JrR1uRsytUFsstALWRQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "On the GT side, {{gtClass:CarpValueClient}} talks to the value host, and the result is a {{gtClass:CarpRemoteValue}}. Opening one asks the running program for its contents, and selecting an item asks it for another live value. And the best part: the views are written in Carp!"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "carpSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "QVtBh/KQSRS2BcVlht7r7w=="
				},
				"code" : "(deftype Point [x Int y Int])\r\r(defview coords [p Point]\r  (=> (NB.text)\r      (NB.title @\"Coords\")\r      (NB.content (fmt \"x: %d, y: %d\" @(Point.x p) @(Point.y p)))))\r\r(Point.init 1 2)"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "mvgxo0nYSJ69XWNW43D9KQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Evaluate that and inspect the point, and you will find a Coords view next to the usual ones. A view is an ordinary function over the value, so it can compute whatever it likes. The standard library types come with views of their own, too: arrays, maps, and friends have structural ones, and a record gets a raw view of its fields for free."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "Rj7yuyHYTHaNSFHXd2WtHA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "On the Pharo side, the remote value is a normal object with views of its own, and there are subclasses for values Pharo can do something with: {{gtClass:CarpRemoteString}} answers a Pharo string, and {{gtClass:CarpRemoteCollection}} fetches its elements, so we can sort and search them in the image. The inspector lets us switch between the Carp side and the Pharo side."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "f2XCRwxkRbWkYEk4qbU/lg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The value host lives until the next evaluation in the session replaces it. An inspector that is still open then points at a program that is gone, which is one of the rough edges we still have to sand down."
			}
		]
	},
